imagine you just picked up your copy of  cyberpunk 2077  and you are just enthralled in the busy  metropolis of night city  you don't even want to play the main  story instead  wandering down each street corner and  entering  every building to see what you can find  while exploring the district of haywood  you take a wrong turn and end up  somewhere you shouldn't be  and suddenly you are surrounded by one  of night city's  dangerous street gangs but it's not the  territorial valentinos  the cyberpsychotic maelstrom or even  the crazed scavengers it's the bozos  a group that's used biosurgery to turn  themselves  into killer clowns and as they step  closer  their large feet slapping the pavement  they all begin to laugh  before one of them plunges a knife into  your gut  okay i should probably clarify before  going any further  no a group of evil killer clowns has  not been confirmed to appear in  cyberpunk 2077  and i highly doubt they will as much as  i  would absolutely love that but the bozos  are a real gang  in the cyberpunk universe in fact there  are a  ton of bizarre and strange groups  written throughout the years for the  pen and paper rpg and that's what we're  going to be talking about today  some of these have had a major presence  in the fiction and others are just  one-off jokes so hopefully you'll get  some good laughs  and who knows maybe one of these groups  will show up in the game  in one form or another let's start by  talking about  prankster gangs groups that are less  concerned with serious organized crime  and more with mischief and mayhem this  nicely brings us back to the group we  started with  the bozos which yes are known as the  ultimate  killer clown organization the bozos  originally just bothered people with  clown related pranks  such as dropping water balloons on them  but after taking on a new leader  known as the great bozo their pranks  became  a lot more deranged as previously  mentioned the bozos aren't dressed like  clowns but turn themselves  into clowns by biosculpting their bodies  with  long feet large red noses and white skin  truly the stuff of nightmares another  prankster gang  is the vamps also known as the  philharmonic vampires  they dress up in tuxedos wear capes and  have  vampire teeth they are by far the most  harmless of the gangs in cyberpunk  doing acts like putting plants inside  convertibles on the street  or making giant naked inflatable dolls  of the governor  no one's really sure what their  motivation is but it mostly seems to be  in good  fun they do have a weird hatred for  mimes though  which puts them at odds with the  juilliard  a defensive gang made up of a collective  of street performers  they formed out of a desire to give  street performers in 2020  some much needed protection their motto  kill a mime  go to jail perhaps a more sympathetic  group  the juilliard are still quite dangerous  with members typically keeping a machine  gun in their viola case  and if you aren't a street performer  under their protection best or clear  their territory  unless you want a juggling club to the  kneecaps  another performance based gang is the  djs  however unlike the juilliard the djs  lack  any real musical talent and are a bunch  of wannabe  rocker boys their racket revolves around  ticket scalping  faking autographs and providing the  occasional muscle protection  everything they do just seems to be a  pretense to try and get themselves  more fame and attention before we move  on i want to mention a couple  other random gangs that didn't really  fit anywhere like the piranhas which is  a  party gang whose only goal is to party  hard  hey excuse me excuse me i don't know why  you don't know this but y'all are  partying in a monster's stomach  thanks i love dancing or the bay area  rapid terror  which is actually a more traditional  gang that isn't that goofy  but i wanted to bring them up because  their name is a reference  to bart san francisco's stinky public  transportation system  but now let's move on to my personal  favorites the poser gangs  groups that model themselves after  famous people or pop culture  a very basic example of a poser gang  would be the western stars  a group that dresses up like wild west  gunslingers and only uses revolvers as  weapons it only gets weirder from there  though  over in nashville is the elvises a  pretty large group where members pose as  elvis during different periods of his  life and whose leader is referred to as  the king  they also claimed to have proof that  elvis lived until 2002.  along the same idea as the elvises we  also got the edisons who all model  themselves after famous inventors  and the kennedys a gang based on the  kennedy family nothing bad  ever happens to the kennedys  and then there's the willow sisterhood  it's made up of a bunch of young women  who are all sculpted to resemble  famous women in history they are also  deadly assassins for hire  speaking of murder there are the jack  the rippers  a gang of serial killers who mimic the  historical murderer of the same name  they even go so far as to wear 18th  century overcoats and  top hats how they haven't been caught is  beyond me  perhaps the most unique of the poser  gangs is the personalities  a gang with no specific theme rather  every member's role is chosen for them  at complete random with no say in what  they can be  roles can be practically any famous  figure from any point in history  after being assigned their new role the  member is biosculpted  to look like that person and they must  stay in character  for the rest of their life poser gangs  aren't just based on real people but  fictional ones as well one of the more  frequently mentioned poster gangs  is the brady bunch a gang that  bio-sculpted themselves to look like  members of the 1970s american sitcom  the brady bunch keeping on the sitcom  train we also have  the gilligans a gay gang where all of  its members base themselves around  characters from gilligan's island  there's also the coneheads based on the  old saturday night live sketch  i am beldar this is primat and connie i  trust we have arrived at the  pre-designated time coordinates  my absolute favorite though has to be  the trekkies  a gang who all model themselves after  star trek  today was another scorcher with a  temperature soaring to new heights the  increased violence between the steel  eagles and trekkies showed that human  temperatures are also running high again  today  the leader of the steel eagle said he  would nail admiral kirk's head to a post  before the end of the week  the police are ready according to police  spokesman james rajid  that's right in the world of cyberpunk  there are people who get  cybernetics to make themselves look like  main characters such as kirk or picard  as well as the many aliens of the show  like vulcans  klingon or borg their home base is  designed to look like a starship  presumably the enterprise and they model  their weapons to look like the classic  star trek phaser  cd project red if you're watching this  please work out a deal with cbs to get  the star trek license for a dlc  add-on it will be the best thing star  trek has done  in years but even if that doesn't happen  i do hope that cd projekt red  embraces the weirder side of cyberpunk's  lore  the original pen and paper game is  simultaneously a dark  harsh take on the future as well as a  tongue-in-cheek satire of american  culture  and i'd like to see some of those  ridiculous gangs make an appearance in  the game  imagine coming across a gang where  everyone is dressed like characters from  i don't know say a popular polish  fantasy franchise it just spin out some  ideas  people there had metal in their heads  waged war from a distance  using things similar to megascopes and  there were no horses  everyone had their own flying ship  instead siri stop fooling around  told you you wouldn't believe me but  that's going to about do it for this  episode in our cyberpunk lore series  the details from these videos was  sourced from our telsorian games  cyberpunk books so see the description  for information if you're interested in  checking those out  and of course check back every week here  on gamespot for a new cyberpunk video  thank you very much for watching  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

